<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leonhard, Count of Gorizia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1440–<a href="/years/1500">1500</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leonhard was the last count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorizia">Gorizia</a> of the Meinhardiner dynasty, ruling from 1462 to 1500. His lands, scattered from the Puster valley to Gorizia, came under pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>. When he died childless in 1500, Emperor Maximilian I inherited Gorizia under an earlier succession treaty, bringing it into the Habsburg lands.</p></div>
